{
 "name": "visiting-hours-house-finish",
 "title": "Visiting Hours: the house's finish options (wallpapers, ceilings, the bezel, higher ceilings) and the height question",
 "subtitle": "Your notes: \"a spread of different choices for the wall pattern, poised towards darker colors, and a pattern for the roof, or maybe something like a bezel for the edges of the roof... Maybe higher roofs as well? ...why are we taller than Lena is?\" Each option is shown in the game from the same spots; nothing is the default until you pick. Mix and match: a wallpaper, a ceiling, a bezel and a height are separate choices (the wallpaper can also differ by room).",
 "questions": [
  "Which wallpaper (1-8), and should every room share it or each room get its own (e.g. damask in the living room, stripe in the hall, sprig in Theo's room)?",
  "Which ceiling: plain, pressed tin, plaster roses, beams, coffers or the starry paper? (Different rooms can differ here too.)",
  "Which bezel where the walls meet the ceiling: the plain strip, a cove, a stepped crown or dentils?",
  "Higher ceilings: as now, +0.4 m or +0.8 m? Higher means she can jump in more rooms, and the attic stairs get longer (or gain a landing).",
  "The attic's underside: plain, painted or dark boards?",
  "Heights: Lena now stands a little taller than Nadia (her eyes 10 cm above Nadia's) and Theo comes to about Nadia's shoulder. Right, or should Lena be taller still (her escape billboard reads about 6'2\")?"
 ],
 "notes": [
  "Why we looked taller than Lena: the stills were taken from 1.6-1.65 m, but Nadia's eye in the game is at 1.5 m (her capsule is 1.7 m). And the cut-outs were sized feet to hair, but the drawings have big heads: Lena's eyes sit 18.6% down her card, so on a 1.72 m card they were at 1.40 m, under Nadia's eye even in the game. Now the stills use 1.5 m and the cut-outs are sized by their eyes: Lena's at 1.60 m (a 1.72 m woman's; her card is 1.97 m), Theo's at 1.20 m (a ten-year-old's; card 1.63 m).",
  "Higher ceilings are a preview (everything from the ceilings up moves up, the walls grow). The movement and stealth values stay; Theo's sightlines don't change (the doorways keep their height). Details in docs/DREAM-HOUSE.md, 'Finish options'.",
  "The wallpaper tiles are drawn by tools/art/vh_house_patterns.py; any of them can be redrawn or recoloured."
 ],
